hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1061","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) became the owner of one hundred shares from Khaybar which he had purchased, and he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I have acquired such wealth that I have never acquired better wealth than this before, and I intend to seek nearness to Allah through it."" Upon this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep the ownership of the garden, and dedicate its fruits in the way of Allah."
"1062","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! I have acquired such wealth from Khaybar that I have never obtained any wealth better or more valuable to me than this. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you wish, keep the ownership of the garden and dedicate its produce in the way of Allah."" So Umar ibn Al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) gave it in charity, then Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) described the manner of his charity."
"1063","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: O Messenger of Allah! I have acquired such wealth that I have never acquired better wealth than this before, and I intend to seek nearness to Allah through it. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Keep its original property with yourself, and give its fruits in charity in the way of Allah."
"1064","It is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever gives 'Umra to someone for him and his heirs, then it will belong to the one for whom 'Umra was made, and it will not return to the giver, because he has given it in such a way that the right of inheritance has been established (i.e., the right of the heirs has been established)."
"1065","It is narrated from Sulaiman bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him) that Tariq gave a ruling in Madinah regarding 'Umra according to the narration of Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet ﷺ."
"1066","It is narrated from Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) made 'Umra' (a type of gift) for the heirs."
"1067","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not give gifts in the manner of 'Umra or Ruqba. Whoever gives something as 'Umra or Ruqba, it will be according to the way of inheritance."
"1068","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever gives something as 'Umra (a type of gift), it belongs to the one to whom it is given."
"1069","It is narrated from Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is given something as 'Umra, it is for him."
